course: dictionary
lesson: 14380
title: Organized: order and plans
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Organized» can mean put in a neat order, or planned and set up. The words around it give you clues about which meaning fits. «She organized her books by size.» Her books are in a neat order, so organized means sorted into groups.
explain: «He organized a party for his friends.» Nobody sorts a party into rows, so here organized means planned and set up. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Arranged or planned would both fit, so that is the meaning.
explain: An organized person keeps things tidy and plans ahead. Some words have more than one meaning, so always check the sentence to see which meaning it uses.
fact: Organized means put in a neat order, or sorted into groups.
fact: Organized also means planned and set up, as in «He organized a party.»
fact: An organized person keeps things tidy and plans ahead.
fact: In maths, data is organized in a table or chart so that patterns are easy to see.
fact: Some British books spell it organised, but it means the same thing.
exercise: «She organized her books by size.» What does organized mean here? | Thrown away | *Put in a neat order | Lost somewhere in the house | Read aloud to the class
exercise: «The class organized a trip to the zoo.» What does organized mean here? | Cancelled and put away | *Planned and set up | Forgotten by everyone | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Sam packs his bag the night before and always knows where his things are. What kind of person is Sam? | Careless | Lazy | Sleepy | *Organized
test: «The teacher organized the results in a table to see the pattern.» What does organized mean here? | Thrown in a pile | Hidden under the desk | *Sorted into a neat order | Lost
test: «The well-organized team won every match.» What does organized suggest? | Messy and noisy | *Planned and working well together | Too tired to play | Late for everything
exam: Which sentence uses organized to mean planned and set up? | «The shelves were full of books.» | «The dog barked all night.» | *«Mum organized a surprise picnic for my birthday.» | «The rain fell on the roof.»
